          players: '5 players (using 25 cards: A-K-Q-J-10-2).',
          deck: '25 cards (Ace to 10, plus a 2 in each suit, and one Joker).',
          equipment: '',
          dealing: 'Each player receives 5 cards. No trump suit.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points by winning exactly 0, 3, or 4 tricks. (Winning 1, 2, or 5 tricks is penalized).',
          gameplay: '1. Must follow suit if possible.\n2. Highest card of led suit wins.\n3. Joker: Can be played on any suit. It wins the trick if led; otherwise, it is neutral (loses).',
          keyRules: [
            'Must follow suit if possible; may play any card if void.',
            'No trumps; highest card of led suit wins the trick.',
            'Deuce led ranks highest in suit, otherwise lowest; Joker led wins the trick, when following it loses.',
            'Object: win exactly 0, 3, or 4 tricks (1, 2, or 5 penalized). Optional bid The Lot to win all five. Game is 25 points.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Identify your 'Void' suit. If you have only 2 cards in a suit, you are likely to be forced to win or lose tricks based on when that suit is led. If you have the Ace and 10 of a suit, aim for 3-4 tricks. If you have only 2s and Jacks, aim for 0.",
          intermediate: "The Joker Lead: Lead the Joker early if you are aiming for 3-4 tricks. This 'uses up' a trick you were guaranteed to win anyway, but it gives you the lead for the next trick where you can play your next lowest card to stay under the 5-trick limit.",
          advanced: 'Social Sabotage: If you see someone has 2 tricks and is trying to lose the rest, lead a suit they must follow with a high card to force them to take a 3rd trick (which they might want) or a 5th trick (which ruins them).',
          tips: [
            "In Minimisere, the 'Middle' (1-2 tricks) is safe but won't win you the game. You must take risks to hit the 3-4 or 0 targets.",
            "Winning 5 tricks without declaring 'The Lot' is the most common mistake for aggressive players.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
